@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# V100.0.153 — Downloads PLAY button audit
+
+## Requested change
+Add a button named `PLAY` to each Downloads item.
+
+## Implemented
+- Version incremented from 100.0.152 to 100.0.153.
+- Added `btn_play` to `item_download.xml` in the existing Downloads action row.
+- PLAY is enabled only when the item is `COMPLETED` and its stored URI is currently readable.
+- PLAY launches the existing SE Player through `PlayerLauncher` with `PlayerType.GENC_MEDIA3`, so it does not depend on any external player selection.
+- The stored local URI is passed unchanged to `PlayerActivity`.
+- Added local URI-aware Media3 data source selection: `content://`, `file://`, and resource-style local schemes use `DefaultDataSource.Factory`; normal IPTV HTTP/HTTPS sources continue to use the existing `DefaultHttpDataSource` path.
+- No APK/Gradle/GitHub build was run.
+
+## Verification
+- `versionCode` = 1000153.
+- `versionName` = 100.0.153.
+- `btn_play` exists in the layout and binding references compile to `btnPlay` by Android View Binding conventions.
+- Downloads adapter binds enabled state and click action.
+- PlayerLauncher receives `playerTypeOverride = PlayerType.GENC_MEDIA3`.
+- PlayerActivity's Genç playback path now selects a local-capable data source for local URIs.
diff --git a/STORAGE_FILE_LOCATION_FIX_V100_0_152_AUDIT.md b/STORAGE_FILE_LOCATION_FIX_V100_0_152_AUDIT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..67d3484
--- /dev/null
+++ b/STORAGE_FILE_LOCATION_FIX_V100_0_152_AUDIT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Storage / File Location Fix — V100.0.152
+
+## Root cause found
+- Downloads default destination used app-specific external storage:
+  `getExternalFilesDir(DIRECTORY_DOWNLOADS)/SE IPTV PLAYER`
+- Recordings used app-specific external storage:
+  `getExternalFilesDirs(null)/SE IPTV PLAYER/Recordings`
+- Android 11+ restricts ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT_TREE from accessing Android/data and its subdirectories, so opening the app-specific folder through DocumentsUI can land in an empty/unusable location.
+
+## New default destinations on Android 10+
+- Downloads: `Download/SE IPTV PLAYER/` via `MediaStore.Downloads` + `RELATIVE_PATH`
+- Recordings: `Movies/SE IPTV PLAYER/Recordings/` via `MediaStore.Video` + `RELATIVE_PATH`
+- `IS_PENDING=1` is used while a new MediaStore file is being written, then published with `IS_PENDING=0` on completion.
+
+## Legacy migration
+- Completed legacy Downloads in the app-specific directory are migrated to MediaStore on opening Downloads.
+- Completed legacy Recordings in the app-specific directory are migrated to MediaStore on opening Records and also when a new recording completes.
+- If migration fails, the original file path is kept so the file is not lost.
+
+## File operations
+- Open File Location uses the public shared folder tree for MediaStore files.
+- Copy/Move from MediaStore sources uses stream-copy fallback, avoiding provider-specific DocumentsContract copy/move behavior.
+- Move deletes the MediaStore source after a successful copy.
+- SAF-selected files/folders keep their existing tree-URI handling.
+
+## Version
+- versionCode: 1000152
+- versionName: 100.0.152
+
+## Build
+- No Gradle build was run.
+- No GitHub build was run.
+
+## Open File Location UX
+- First attempts `ACTION_VIEW` on a `Document.MIME_TYPE_DIR` URI for the exact shared folder.
+- Falls back to `ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT_TREE` with `EXTRA_INITIAL_URI` when the device's file manager does not expose direct folder viewing.
